      "problem": "If $f(x)$ is right-continuous at $x=2$ and ${lim}_{x\\to {2}^{+}}f(x)=-1,$ then what is ${lim}_{x\\to {2}^{+}}(f(x)+f(2))?$",
      "worked_solution": "Since $f(x)$ is right-continuous at $x=2,$ we must have\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to {2}^{+}}f(x)=f(2)=-1.\n$$\n\nConsequently,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to {2}^{+}}(f(x)+f(2)) & ={lim}_{x\\to {2}^{+}}f(x)+f(2) \\\\  & =-1-1 \\\\  & =-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
